THOUGHT: TextField’s constructors call initialize(), which TextArea overrides to initialize linesBreak. However, TextArea’s constructors don’t call initialize(), so NullAway flags that linesBreak (non-null by default) may not be initialized. The minimal, behavior-preserving fix is to ensure all TextArea constructors delegate to a single constructor that calls super(...) (which already calls initialize()) or explicitly call initialize() after super. Since TextField’s constructor already calls initialize(), I’ll just chain TextArea constructors so only one calls super, avoiding duplicate initialization and satisfying NullAway. Then I’ll run the compile task to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '63,73c\  public TextArea(String text, Skin skin) {
    this(text, skin.get(TextFieldStyle.class));
  }

  public TextArea(String text, Skin skin, String styleName) {
    this(text, skin.get(styleName, TextFieldStyle.class));
  }

  public TextArea(String text, TextFieldStyle style) {
    super(text, style);
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/TextArea.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:|error: \[NullAway\]" -n new_build_output.log | head && grep -n "errors" new_build_output.log | tail
```

